-boundary.test.ts:365:    // poke — the background drain ran and the summaries landed ready.\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts:409:    // The advance ran before the throwing poke: position = the older turn.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/coverage.md:28:| AC-4.1 | Story 5 | real-suite ran/not-ran accounting and real host |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/coverage.md:29:| AC-4.2 | Story 5 | real-adapter capstone |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/coverage.md:31:| TC-4.2 | Story 5 | lifecycle capstone |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/coverage.md:60:| Real endpoint exercises same seam | Story 5 | TC-4.1, TC-4.3 | OpenRouter host conforms to `ModelCall` and routing helpers |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/coverage.md:61:| Real adapter completes lifecycle capstone | Story 5 | TC-4.2 | all derivations ready with real provenance and coherent checkpoints |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/coverage.md:63:| Boundary eviction respects whole turns and target landing | Story 6 | TC-5.2 | groups flip whole-turn oldest-first and land in target range |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/coverage.md:76:| 5. Real-Inference Suite and Capstone | fixture / packaging + capstone integration | The same host function seam is proven against a real endpoint and lifecycle exercise. | capstone plus seam conformance | auth-gated run, external endpoint, capstone integration | Keep: suite accounting is inseparable from real endpoint proof. |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/coverage.md:77:| 6. Turn-End Boundary Advance | semantic rule / contract patch | Visibility boundary movement is turn-close-owned and whole-turn-grained. | config change plus regression amendments | transition-state atomicity, replay determinism, Epic 03 test amendments | Keep: trigger, grouping, config, 