specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:25:- **AC-4.2**: The capstone: the Epic 04 lifecycle sequence with the real adapter completes with every derivation kind landing `ready` at least once — non-empty content, no deterministic-marker strings, provenance naming the real model — and the deterministic leg's checkpoint-coherence assertions hold structurally (cleared-then-ready around mutations; second compact reflects post-edit content).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:30:  - with `LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY`, each of the seven kinds round-trips real inference once\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:32:  - with the key absent in a controlled leg, the suite emits a not-ran record with reason\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:33:  - the not-ran record is distinguishable from a pass\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:34:  - the suite-level guard emits exactly one ran/not-ran line into run output\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:52:This story proves the same `ModelCall` seam against a real endpoint without making CI depend on network credentials. The OpenRouter function is test-owned host code, not production LHC transport code, and exists to prove that the injected-function contract is sufficient.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:54:The capstone reuses the Epic 04 lifecycle sequence with real-adapter structural assertions: ready forms, non-marker content, real-model provenance, mutation regeneration, and coherent checkpoints.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:61:- The story has an external endpoint, auth-gated execution, visible accounting, and a capstone path spanning intake, drain, compact, mutation, rebuild, and materialization.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:62:- The not-ran path is as important as the keyed path because silent pass is the failure mode.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:66:- The suite guard must report one visible ran/not-ran fact.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:96:| TC-4.1 | `test/inference-real.test.ts` | keyed seven-kind real round-trips; unkeyed not-ran record; exactly one suite-level ran/not-ran output line |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:98:| TC-4.3 | `test/inference-real.test.ts` | OpenRouter host passes shared `ModelCall` contract and SDK routing helpers |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:104:| Silent real-suite skip | `test/inference-real.test.ts` unkeyed guard leg | Not-ran record has reason and cannot look like pass | A skipped keyed suite could leave default CI green without proving anything |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:105:| Fixture does not represent host boundary | `test/fixtures/seam-conformance.ts` helpers | Same contract/routing helpers run against fake and real host functions | A direct OpenRouter call could pass while violating the SDK boundary shape |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:127:| `LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY` | opt-in suite only | suite reports ran or not-ran |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:128:| `LHC_OPENROUTER_MODEL` | opt-in suite optional | fixture default used when unset |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:135:| `test/fixtures/openrouter-call.ts` | `createOpenRouterCall(key, defaultModel)` implements `ModelCall` over OpenRouter using plain `fetch` |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:136:| `resolveRealSuiteEnv()` | returns `{ key, model }` or `{ notRan: reason }` |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:139:OpenRouter failure mapping:\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:149:The CI-default suite makes zero network calls. The keyed run is recorded in story completion notes with date, model, and pass state.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:153:- `LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY` controls keyed execution.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:154:- `LHC_OPENROUTER_MODEL` may select the cheap model; fixture default applies when unset.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:155:- OpenRouter provider/model interpretation is host-side and still returns the AC-1.2 `ModelCallResult` shape.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:167:- Registration/default path: env-gated suite in default runner reports ran/not-ran; keyed execution reaches OpenRouter through plain `fetch`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:168:- Evidence: keyed seven-kind round-trips, shared seam-conformance helpers, and real-adapter lifecycle capstone.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:183:- OpenRouter-backed test `ModelCall` fixture exists and confor