\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Both gates are green. Summary:\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n**`src/inference/adapter.ts`** — `boundContent` had one path that violated its own invariant: when `maxInputChars` was smaller than the truncation marker, `Math.max(0, maxInputChars - marker.length)` clamped `keep` to 0, so the function returned the marker alone — whose length exceeds `maxInputChars`. Replaced the silent clamp with an explicit guard: when the marker can't fit the budget, degrade to a plain head truncation (`content.slice(0, maxInputChars)`) that honors the cap exactly. For all normal inputs (marker fits), behavior is unchanged — `keep` is now guaranteed non-negative without the `Math.max`.\\n\\n## Test\\n\\n**`test/inference-prompts.test.ts`** — added a focused case under the existing DD-7 bounding block using `maxInputChars: 40` (a valid-but-small budget below the ~78-char marker — the counterexample). It asserts the bounded whole stays `≤ 40`, is a true prefix of the input (head-only degradation), and carries no marker text. This case fails against the pre-fix code (it returned the ~78-char marker), so it's a real regression guard.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- **Targeted Story 3 tests** (`vitest run test/inference-adapter.test.ts test/inference-prompts.test.ts`): 26/26 passed.\\n- **Configured story gate** (`pnpm run verify` = `red-verify` build/typecheck/lint/boundaries + full `vitest run`): 37 files, 353/353 passed. (The `boundary advance failed …` line is a fault-injection test emitting its expected message, not a failure.)\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1670,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":40312,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1670},\"output_tokens\":2,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},