pts manifest re-record matches HEAD content exactly (git diff shows no change to the test file itself), (3) Epic 02 derivation suites green untouched (verify-all 365/365). Then Story 5 (real suite + capstone) per chunk order.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/04-failure-classification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:607:Caller implication: Treat this as startup bookkeeping only; wait for the first planner transition before routing work.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/04-failure-classification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:624:Meaning: The child result or terminal decision is being written to durable artifacts before the next transition.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/04-failure-classification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:651:Meaning: The run stopped before a planned transition finished, usually because the caller or runtime interrupted it.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:4:You are the story lead for `05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone` on durable story run `05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone-story-run-001`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:19:Path: /Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:27:Add the opt-in OpenRouter-backed suite with visible ran/not-ran accounting and the real-adapter lifecycle capstone.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:34:**Objective:** Verify all seven derivation kinds and the Epic 04 lifecycle sequence through a real endpoint when keyed, with explicit not-ran accounting when unkeyed.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:36:**Scope In:** Test-owned OpenRouter `ModelCall`, suite guard, ran/not-ran output, seven real round-trips, shared seam-conformance assertions, and lifecycle capstone structural checks.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:45:- **AC-4.1**: The real-inference suite is opt-in on key presence and its outcome is always visible: ran (with the model assignments used) or not-ran (with reason) in the suite output. Absence of the key can never produce a silent pass. The suite's model-call function lives in test code, implements the AC-1.2 contract, and reaches a real endpoint.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:46:- **AC-4.2**: The capstone: the Epic 04 lifecycle sequence with the real adapter completes with every derivation kind landing `ready` at least once — non-empty content, no deterministic-marker strings, provenance naming the real model — and the deterministic leg's checkpoint-coherence assertions hold structurally (cleared-then-ready around mutations; second compact reflects post-edit content).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:51:  - with `LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY`, each of the seven kinds round-trips real inference once\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:53:  - with the key absent in a controlled leg, the suite emits a not-ran record with reason\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:54:  - the not-ran record is distinguishable from a pass\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:55:  - the suite-level guard emits exactly one ran/not-ran line into run output\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:73:This story proves the same `ModelCall` seam against a real endpoint without making CI depend on network credentials. The OpenRouter function is test-owned host code, not production LHC transport code, and exists to prove that the injected-function contract is sufficient.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:75:The capstone reuses the Epic 04 lifecycle sequence with real-adapter structural assertions: ready forms, non-marker content, real-model provenance, mutation regeneration, and coherent checkpoints.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:82:- The story has an external endpoint, auth-gated execution, visible accounting, and a capstone path spanning intake, drain, compact, mutation, rebuild, and materialization.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:83:- The not-ran path is as important as the keyed path because silent pass is the failure mode.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:87:- The suite guard must report one visible ran/not-ran fact.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:117:| TC-4.1 | `test/inference-real.test.ts` | keyed seven-kind real round-trips; unkeyed not-ran record; exactly one suite-level ran/not-ran output line |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:119:| TC-4.3 | `test/inference-real.test.ts` | OpenRouter host passes shared `ModelCall` contract and SDK routing helpers |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:125:| Silent real-suite skip | `test/inference-real.test.ts` unkeyed guard leg | Not-ran record has reason and cannot look like pass | A skipped keyed suite could leave default CI green without proving anything |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:126:| Fixture does not represent host boundary | `test/fixtures/seam-conformance.ts` helpers | Same contract/routing helpers run against fake and real host functions | A direct OpenRouter call could pass while violating the SDK boundary shape |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:148:| `LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY` | opt-in suite only | suite reports ran or not-ran |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:149:| `LHC_OPENROUTER_MODEL` | opt-in suite optional | fixture default used when unset |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:156:| `test/fixtures/openrouter-call.ts` | `createOpenRouterCall(key, defaultModel)` implements `ModelCall` over OpenRouter using plain `fetch` |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:157:| `resolveRealSuiteEnv()` | returns `{ key, model }` or `{ notRan: reason }` |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:160:OpenRouter failure mapping:\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:170:The CI-default suite makes zero network calls. The keyed run is recorded in story completion notes with date, model, and pass state.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:174:- `LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY` controls keyed execution.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:175:- `LHC_OPENROUTER_MODEL` may select the cheap model; fixture default applies when unset.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:176:- OpenRouter provider/model interpretation is host-side and still returns the AC-1.2 `ModelCallResult` shape.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:188:- Registration/default path: env-gated suite in default runner reports ran/not-ran; keyed execution reaches OpenRouter through plain `fetch`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:189:- Evidence: keyed seven-kind round-trips, shared seam-conformance helpers, and real-adapter lifecycle capstone.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-plan