ead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:528:      - \"For a legal zone with a newest closed turn followed by one or more turnless singleton groups, is the `[target, target + one turn)` landing guarantee allowed to have an exception so the newest closed turn remains protected?\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:664:    recommendedNextStep: \"Story verification pass, then epic-level review: with Story 6 done all six stories of Epic 05 are implemented, so the epic closeout (deviation table including the recorded keyed real-inference run, doc alignment, final gate) is next\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:902:      rationale: \"Approved: AC-5.3's protections are authoritative over the landing window when they conflict. The spec itself already contains this precedent — TC-5.2 requires the newest closed turn to remain intact even when it alone exceeds target, which necessarily lands the zone above target + one turn. Trailing turnless singleton groups positioned after the newest closed turn cannot be evicted without first evicting the protected newest turn, because the boundary is a positional marker advanced oldest-first; their protection is structural, not a new rule. Therefore the landing guarantee [target, target + one turn) applies only when achievable without violating the explicit protections. Keep current implementation and tests; update AC-5.3/tech-design wording to state the exception explicitly; rerun verification. This ruling will be surfaced at epic review for ratification.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:921:rationale: \"Approved: AC-5.3's protections are authoritative over the landing window when they conflict. The spec itself already contains this precedent — TC-5.2 requires the newest closed turn to remain intact even when it alone exceeds target, which necessarily lands the zone above target + one turn. Trailing turnless singleton groups positioned after the newest closed turn cannot be evicted without first evicting the protected newest turn, because the boundary is a positional marker advanced oldest-first; their protection is structural, not a new rule. Therefore the landing guarantee [target, target + one turn) applies only when achievable without violating the explicit protections. Keep current implementation and tests; update AC-5.3/tech-design wording to state the exception explicitly; rerun verification. This ruling will be surfaced at epic review for ratification.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:1187:Caller implication: Treat this as startup bookkeeping only; wait for the first planner transition before routing work.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:1204:Meaning: The child result or terminal decision is being written to durable artifacts before the next transition.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:1231:Meaning: The run stopped before a planned transition finished, usually because the caller or runtime interrupted it.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:55:  - SDK-coverage comparison is a story-completion check: suite files and domain-operation coverage unchanged from pre-deletion, process suites excepted\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:76:- The implementation is mostly deletion and export cleanup, but public API and test-suite deletio