avior but keyed run evidence is still absent, do not accept; request ruling or block on the missing keyed proof required by the story DoD.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:779:  storyRunId: \"05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone-story-run-001\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:785:    note: \"If verifier passes unkeyed/default behavior but keyed run evidence is still absent, do not accept; request ruling or block on the missing keyed proof required by the story DoD.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:790:  storyRunId: \"05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone-story-run-001\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:795:  artifact: \"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/004-verify.json\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:815:Caller implication: Treat this as startup bookkeeping only; wait for the first planner transition before routing work.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:832:Meaning: The child result or terminal decision is being written to durable artifacts before the next transition.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:859:Meaning: The run stopped before a planned transition finished, usually because the caller or runtime interrupted it.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:182:| message-grained eviction goldens | re-cut for turn grouping | eviction granularity is whole turn |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:186:Lifecycle/capstone deterministic legs from Epic 04 are untouched. Red-manifest regeneration is required after applying the amendment ledger.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:188:#### Transition-State Risk\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:250:| `test/inference-real.test.ts` | opt-in (`LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY`) | TC-4.1, TC-4.2, TC-4.3 |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:268:**`test/fixtures/openrouter-call.ts`** (Chunk 5) — the real host: `createOpenRouterCall(key, defaultModel)` → `ModelCall` over `fetch` to OpenRouter's OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint; implements the exact `ModelCall` contract (OpenRouter takes one model slug, so the fixture resolves the `provider`+`model` routing keys into that slug — the host-side interpretation AC-1.2 grants), maps HTTP 401/403 → `auth`, 429 → `rate_limit`, 400 → `invalid_request`, network errors → `network`, everything else → `other`, and extracts non-empty assistant text into the `ModelCallResult` success shape. `resolveRealSuiteEnv()` → `{ key, model } | { notRan: reason }`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:328:- unkeyed (controlled: suite re-invoked with key stripped from env in a subprocess-free way — the guard function called directly with empty env) → `notRan` record with reason; assert the record's shape and that it is not a pass\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:329:- the suite-level guard emits exactly one ran/not-ran line into the run output\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:338:- `assertModelCallContract(openRouterCall)` and `assertRoutingThroughSdk(openRouterCall, realAssignments)` — the same helpers TC-1.2 ran against the fake, unchanged (DD-13)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:365:- full default suite green is the suite run itself; the SDK-coverage comparison is a one-time story-completion check recorded in the story DoD (suite files and their domain-operation coverage unchanged from pre-deletion, process files excepted)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:380:| message-grained eviction goldens (G1 as cut for Epic 03) | re-cut for turn grouping | eviction granularity (AC-5.2) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:384:Lifecycle/capstone deterministic legs (Epic 04's exercise) are untouched: they run the deterministic provider and never asserted boundary trigger timing.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:397:| 5: Real suite | `inference-real` (guard testable unkeyed) | OpenRouter fixture, accounting guard, capstone leg | unkeyed: not-ran record asserted in CI; keyed: TC-4.1–4.3 green locally (run recorded in story DoD with model used) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:400:**Story-completion accounting for Chunk 5:** the keyed run cannot gate CI (no secret in CI by design). The story's DoD requires a recorded keyed run — date, model, pass state — in the deviation/completion notes. A keyed run that has never happened blocks epic acceptance: the capstone is the integration-readiness gate, and an unexercised gate is the silent-skip failure mode this suite exists to prevent.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:410:| Silent real-suite skip | TC-4.1's unkeyed leg asserts the not-ran record exists and is not a pass |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:593:    recommendedNextStep: \"Story verification pass, then epic-level review: with Story 6 done all six stories of Epic 05 are implemented, so the epic closeout (deviation table including the recorded keyed real-inference run, doc alignment, final gate) is next\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:862:      - \"No fake adapter, shim, placeholder branch, hidden floorTokens fallback, or non-real boundary advance surface was found in the reviewed production files.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:867:      - \"For a legal zone with a newest closed turn followed by one or more turnless singleton groups, is the `[target, target + one turn)` landing guarantee allowed to have an exception so the newest closed turn remains protected?\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:950:      rationale: \"Approved: AC-5.3's protections are authoritative over the landing window when they conflict. The spec itself already contains this precedent — TC-5.2 requires the newest closed turn to remain intact even when it alone exceeds target, which necessarily lands the zone above target + one turn. Trailing turnless singleton groups positioned after the newest closed turn cannot be evicted without first evicting the protected newest turn, because the boundary is a positional marker advanced oldest-first; their protection is structural, not a new rule. Therefore the landing guarantee [target, target + one turn) applies only when achievable without violating the explicit protections. Keep current implementation and tests; update AC-5.3/tech-design wording to state the exception explicitly; rerun verification. This ruling will be surfaced at epic review for ratification.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:969:rationale: \"Approved: AC-5.3's protections are authoritative over the landing window when they conflict. The spec itself already contains this precedent — TC-5.2 requires the newest closed turn to remain intact even when it alone exceeds target, which necessarily lands the zone above target + one turn. Trailing turnless singleton groups positioned after the newest closed turn cannot be evicted without first evicting the protected newest turn, because the boundary is a positional marker advanced oldest-first; their protection is structural, not a new rule. Therefore the landing guarantee [target, target + one turn) applies only when achievable without violating the explicit protections. Keep current implementation and tests; update AC-5.3/tech-design wording to state the exception explicitly; rerun verification. This ruling will be surfaced at epic review for ratification.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:1281:Caller implication: Treat this as startup bookkeeping only; wait for the first planner transition before routing work.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:1298:Meaning: The child result or terminal decision is being written to durable artifacts before the next transition.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:1325:Meaning: The run stopped before a planned transition finished, usually because the caller or runtime interrupted it.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/003-quick-fix.stdout.log:29:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01XuNJf4SPafL6vVeyg2agkn\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t# Story 6: Turn-End Boundary Advance\\n2\\t\\n3\\t### Summary\\n4\\t<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\\n5\\t\\n6\\tPatch the Epic 03 visibility boundary to advance only at turn close, evict whole turns, and retire floor-token config.\\n7\\t\\n8\\t### Description\\n9\\t<!-- Jira: Description field -->\\n10\\t\\n11\\t**User Profile:** The operator needs stable reads during an open turn and predictable boundary movement after the turn closes.\\n12\\t\\n13\\t**Objective:** Move boundary advance from after every intake commit to turn close while preserving Epic 03's remaining visibility contracts.\\n14\\t\\n15\\t**Scope In:** Turn-end trigger gate, whole-turn eviction, peek-ahead stop, newest-closed-turn protection, two-field visibility config, Epic 03 test amendment ledger, and red-manifest regeneration.\\n16\\t\\n17\\t**Scope Out:** Mid-turn safety ceiling and any inference behavior.\\n18\\t\\n19\\t**Dependencies:** Independent of Stories 2-5. Uses POC commits `1cf2dc45`, `6a9aa7a4`, and `f12a850d` as reference implementation.\\n20\\t\\n21\\t### Acceptance Criteria\\n22\\t<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\\n23\\t\\n24\\t- **AC-5.1**: The advance check runs only when an intake batch commits a `turn_end`. Mid-turn batches never move the boundary regardless of zone size, and rendered bytes do not change between turn closes.\\n25\\t- **AC-5.2**: Eviction is whole-turn, oldest-first: an advance flips every tool result in each evicted turn together; no turn is ever partially flipped.\\n26\\t- **AC-5.3**: The peek-ahead stop: a turn is evicted only if the zone's sum after evicting it remains ≥ target. The advance lands in [target, target + one turn). The newest closed turn is never evicted.\\n27\\t- **AC-5.4**: Config is max and target with defaults 64k/32k; max > target validated with a caller error; the floor token budget is retired from the config surface.\\n28\\t- **AC-5.5**: All other Epic 03 boundary contracts hold under the new trigger: forward-only, summary-else-truncation short form, compact reset, deterministic replay, post-commit seam with non-blocking failure visible in status.\\n29\\t\\n30\\t**Test Conditions**\\n31\\t\\n32\\t- **TC-5.1** (AC-5.1, AC-5.2): `view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts`\\n33\\t  - mid-turn batches accumulate tool results past max; boundary remains unmoved\\n34\\t  - consecutive pulls during the open turn are byte-identical\\n35\\t  - the batch closing the turn commits; exactly one advance runs\\n36\\t  - flipped set is whole oldest turns, with every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together\\n37\\t  - no turn is partially flipped\\n38\\t  - a small next turn closes under max and causes no movement\\n39\\t  - turnless tool result evicts as a singleton group\\n40\\t- **TC-5.2** (AC-5.3, AC-5.4): `view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts`\\n41\\t  - golden G2: 30k/25k/20k/15k turns with 64k/32k budgets advances boundary after the 25k group and lands zone at 35k\\n42\\t  - landing always falls in [target, target + one turn)\\n43\\t  - exact-target variant advances through a turn when remaining sum is exactly target\\n44\\t  - newest closed turn remains intact even when it alone exceeds target\\n45\\t  - `maxTokens <= targetTokens` returns a caller `TypeError` naming the constraint\\n46\\t  - defaults resolve to 64k/32k\\n47\\t- **TC-5.3** (AC-5.5): amended `view-boundary.test.ts` plus new turn-end file\\n48\\t  - flipped results stay flipped across later turn closes\\n49\\t  - short form remains summary-when-ready else truncation\\n50\\t  - compact resets boundary to the compact point with a fresh full tail\\n51\\t  - same record plus same budgets replays to identical boundary trajectory\\n52\\t  - injected `post-commit-advance` failure leaves intake unaffected, boundary unchanged, and status showing over-budget zone\\n53\\t  - the next turn close heals the failed advance\\n54\\t\\n55\\t### Technical Design\\n56\\t<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\\n57\\t\\n58\\t#### Architecture Context\\n59\\t\\n60\\tThis story patches Epic 03's visibility-boundary contract. The advance registration stays on the existing post-commit seam but is gated to batches that commit a `turn_end`; the decision function changes from message-grained eviction plus floor config to whole-turn groups plus peek-ahead target landing.\\n61\\t\\n62\\tThe storage shape does not migrate. `view_boundary` remains the stored boundary; `VisibilityBudgets` loses `floorTokens`, and the newest closed turn plus open-turn trigger rule replaces the old floor behavior.\\n63\\t\\n64\\t#### Build Strategy\\n65\\t\\n66\\tStrategy: full-staged-risk\\n67\\t\\n68\\tReason:\\n69\\t- This changes a persisted read boundary, replay determinism, config validation, and an existing Epic 03 test surface.\\n70\\t- The amendment ledger must be applied precisely so superseded tests are rewritten, not discarded.\\n71\\t\\n72\\tRisk Reminders:\\n73\\t- Keep post-commit ordering and throw isolation unchanged.\\n74\\t- Use whole-turn grouping by `turn_id`; turnless results become singleton groups.\\n75\\t- Regenerate the red-manifest artifact after ledger amendments.\\n76\\t\\n77\\t#### Implementation Targets\\n78\\t\\n79\\t| Area | Files / Modules |\\n80\\t|---|---|\\n81\\t| Intake post-commit gate | `src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts` |\\n82\\t| Boundary decision | `src/domains/thread-view/internal/boundary.ts` |\\n83\\t| Visibility config | `src/shared/view.ts`, config resolution code |\\n84\\t| Boundary fixtures | `test/fixtures/` boundary helpers including `seedTurnedToolResults(...)` |\\n85\\t| Story-owned tests | `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts`, amended `test/view-boundary.test.ts` |\\n86\\t| Red-manifest artifact | project red-manifest artifact used by the house Red/Green flow |\\n87\\t\\n88\\t#### Design References\\n89\\t\\n90\\t- [epic.md §Flow 5](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/epic.md:151), lines 151-171\\n91\\t- [epic.md §Data Contracts](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/epic.md:238), line 238\\n92\\t- [tech-design.md §Design Decisions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:28), lines 28-30\\n93\\t- [tech-design.md §Top-Tier Surfaces](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:41), lines 41-42\\n94\\t- [tech-design.md §Module Responsibility Matrix](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:95), lines 95-97\\n95\\t- [tech-design.md §Flow 5](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:175), lines 175-197\\n96\\t- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:272), lines 272-275\\n97\\t- [test-plan.md §Boundary fixtures](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/test-plan.md:38), line 38\\n98\\t- [test-plan.md §TC-5.1 / TC-5.2 / TC-5.3](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/test-plan.md:106), lines 106-125\\n99\\t- [test-plan.md §Epic 03 Test Amendment Ledger](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/test-plan.md:138), lines 138-150\\n100\\t- [test-plan.md §Red/Green per Chunk](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/test-plan.md:164), line 164\\n101\\t- [coverage.md §Story Shape Review](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/coverage.md:77), line 77\\n102\\t\\n103\\t#### Test Mapping\\n104\\t\\n105\\t| TC | Test File / Check | Test Description |\\n106\\t|---|---|---|\\n107\\t| TC-5.1 | `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` | mid-turn batches do not move boundary; turn close advances once; whole oldest turns flip; turnless singleton leg |\\n108\\t| TC-5.2 | `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` | G2 peek-ahead landing, exact-target leg, newest-turn protection, `maxTokens > targetTokens`, 64k/32k defaults |\\n109\\t| TC-5.3 | amended `test/view-boundary.test.ts` plus new turn-end file | monotonicity, short form, compact reset, deterministic replay, failure injection, next-close heal |\\n110\\t\\n111\\t#### Architecture-Risk Tests\\n112\\t\\n113\\t| Risk | Test File / Check | Test Description | Why AC/TC Mapping Alone Would Miss It |\\n114\\t|---|---|---|---|\\n115\\t| Boundary decision and status sum diverge | amended boundary tests | Status `zoneTokens` and advance decision use the same population after advances and failures | ACs state behavior; this proves two readers do not drift |\\n116\\t| Superseded Epic 03 tests deleted wholesale | amendment ledger plus red-manifest regeneration | Each named old leg is inverted, replaced, re-cut, or kept | Green tests alone would not prove the sanctioned test-change path was followed |\\n117\\t| Partial-turn eviction | `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` per-turn all-or-nothing assertions | Every tool result in an evicted turn flips together | Boundary position could appear correct while a turn is split internally |\\n118\\t\\n119\\t#### Technical Notes\\n120\\t\\n121\\tRelevant contracts:\\n122\\t\\n123\\t```ts\\n124\\texport interface VisibilityBudgets {\\n125\\t  maxTokens: number;\\n126\\t  targetTokens: number;\\n127\\t}\\n128\\t\\n129\\t// defaults: { maxTokens: 64_000, targetTokens: 32_000 }\\n130\\t// validation: maxTokens > targetTokens\\n131\\t```\\n132\\t\\n133\\tBoundary decision:\\n134\\t\\n135\\t```text\\n136\\tadvanceDecision(groups, { maxTokens, targetTokens }):\\n137\\t  total <= maxTokens -> no movement\\n138\\t  walk groups oldest-first, stopping before the newest closed turn\\n139\\t    (the newest closed turn and any trailing turnless singletons after it\\n140\\t     are never candidates; with no closed turn present, exclude the newest\\n141\\t     group instead)\\n142\\t  evict group only if (remaining - group.tokenSum) >= targetTokens\\n143\\t  boundary position = highest source_event_order in last evicted group\\n144\\t```\\n145\\t\\n146\\tGrouping rules:\\n147\\t\\n148\\t| Case | Grouping |\\n149\\t|---|---|\\n150\\t| normal turned tool results | group by `turn_id`, oldest first by lowest `source_event_order` |\\n151\\t| `turn_id IS NULL` | singleton group |\\n152\\t| newest closed turn | never candidate for eviction |\\n153\\t| open turn | structurally untouchable because checks only run on turn close |\\n154\\t\\n155\\tEpic 03 test amendment ledger:\\n156\\t\\n157\\t| Existing test area | Change | Reason |\\n158\\t|---|---|---|\\n159\\t| floor-protection legs | superseded and replaced by newest-turn-protection legs in TC-5.2 | `floorTokens` retired |\\n160\\t| per-intake-advance legs | inverted into TC-5.1 mid-turn-never-moves assertions | trigger moved to turn close |\\n161\\t| message-grained eviction goldens | re-cut for turn grouping | eviction granularity is whole turn |\\n162\\t| construction tests passing `floorTokens` | update to two-field budgets; add new rejected-unknown-config test for `floorTokens` | config surface change |\\n163\\t| status `zoneTokens` legs | unchanged | shared-query invariant holds |\\n164\\t\\n165\\tLifecycle/capstone deterministic legs from Epic 04 are untouched. Red-manifest regeneration is required after applying the amendment ledger.\\n166\\t\\n167\\t#### Transition-State Risk\\n168\\t\\n169\\t- Mid-turn state may exceed max and remain full until the turn closes.\\n170\\t- The open turn is untouchable because no check runs mid-turn.\\n171\\t- The newest closed turn is never evicted, even when oversized.\\n172\\t- A failed post-commit advance must leave intake committed and status visibly over budget until the next turn close heals it.\\n173\\t\\n174\\t#### Anti-Shim Requirements\\n175\\t\\n176\\t- Do not keep a hidden `floorTokens` fallback.\\n177\\t- Do not move the advance seam; gate the existing post-commit registration.\\n178\\t- Do not evict individual messages from a turned group.\\n179\\t- Do not delete Epic 03 tests without applying the ledger and regenerating the red-manifest artifact.\\n180\\t\\n181\\t#### Production Path Proof\\n182\\t\\n183\\t- Entrypoint: intake-stream commit pipeline.\\n184\\t- Registration/default path: existing post-commit advance registration, gated by committed `turn_end`.\\n185\\t- Evidence: turn-end boundary tests assert no mid-turn movement, one advance at close, deterministic replay, and non-blocking failure visibility.\\n186\\t\\n187\\t#### Verification\\n188\\t\\n189\\t- Targeted: `cd packages/lhc && pnpm exec vitest run test/view-boundary.test.ts test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts`\\n190\\t- Story gate: `cd packages/lhc && pnpm run red-verify && pnpm exec vitest run test/view-boundary.test.ts test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts`\\n191\\t- Epic gate: `cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify-all`\\n192\\t\\n193\\t#### Spec Deviations\\n194\\t\\n195\\tNone.\\n196\\t\\n197\\t### Definition of Done\\n198\\t<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n199\\t\\n200\\t- Advance registration runs only for batches that committed `turn_end`.\\n201\\t- Boundary eviction groups tool results by turn and flips whole groups oldest-first.\\n202\\t- Peek-ahead stop and newest-closed-turn protection match TC-5.2.\\n203\\t- `floorTokens` is removed from the visibility config surface; defaults and `maxTokens > targetTokens` validation are updated.\\n204\\t- Epic 03 amended tests are changed according to the ledger, not deleted wholesale.\\n205\\t- Red manifest is regenerated after the test amendments.\\n206\\t- TC-5.1, TC-5.2, and TC-5.3 are green.\\n207\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"c6fd1fc9-717e-4718-8050-43c47347ff45\",\"uuid\":\"0bc9e039-a89b-432d-b1d9-f0a7ce39fbfb\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-13T00:13:14.966Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md\",\"content\":\"# Story 6: Turn-End Boundary Advance\\n\\n### Summary\\n<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\\n\\nPatch the Epic 03 visibility boundary to advance only at turn close, evict whole turns, and retire floor-token config.\\n\\n### Description\\n<!-- Jira: Description field -->\\n\\n**User Profile:** The operator needs stable reads during an open turn and predictable boundary movement after the turn closes.\\n\\n**Objective:** Move boundary advance from after every intake commit to turn close while preserving Epic 03's remaining visibility contracts.\\n\\n**Scope In:** Turn-end trigger gate, whole-turn eviction, peek-ahead stop, newest-closed-turn protection, two-field visibility config, Epic 03 test amendment ledger, and red-manifest regeneration.\\n\\n**Scope Out:** Mid-turn safety ceiling and any inference behavior.\\n\\n**Dependencies:** Independent of Stories 2-5. Uses POC commits `1cf2dc45`, `6a9aa7a4`, and `f12a850d` as reference implementation.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\\n\\n- **AC-5.1**: The advance check runs only when an intake batch commits a `turn_end`. Mid-turn batches never move the boundary regardless of zone size, and rendered bytes do not change between turn closes.\\n- **AC-5.2**: Eviction is whole-turn, oldest-first: an advance flips every tool result in each evicted turn together; no turn is ever partially flipped.\\n- **AC-5.3**: The peek-ahead stop: a turn is evicted only if the zone's sum after evicting it remains ≥ target. The advance lands in [target, target + one turn). The newest closed turn is never evicted.\\n- **AC-5.4**: Config is max and target with defaults 64k/32k; max > target validated with a caller error; the floor token budget is retired from the config surface.\\n- **AC-5.5**: All other Epic 03 boundary contracts hold under the new trigger: forward-only, summary-else-truncation short form, compact reset, deterministic replay, post-commit seam with non-blocking failure visible in status.\\n\\n**Test Conditions**\\n\\n- **TC-5.1** (AC-5.1, AC-5.2): `view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts`\\n  - mid-turn batches accumulate tool results past max; boundary remains unmoved\\n  - consecutive pulls during the open turn are byte-identical\\n  - the batch closing the turn commits; exactly one advance runs\\n  - flipped set is whole oldest turns, with every tool result in each evicted turn flipped together\\n  - no turn is partially flipped\\n  - a small next turn closes under max and causes no movement\\n  - turnless tool result evicts as a singleton group\\n- **TC-5.2** (AC-5.3, AC-5.4): `view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts`\\n  - golden G2: 30k/25k/20k/15k turns with 64k/32k budgets advances boundary after the 25k group and lands zone at 35k\\n  - landing always falls in [target, target + one turn)\\n  - exact-target variant advances through a turn when remaining sum is exactly target\\n  - newest closed turn remains intact even when it alone exceeds target\\n  - `maxTokens <= targetTokens` returns a caller `TypeError` naming the constraint\\n  - defaults resolve to 64k/32k\\n- **TC-5.3** (AC-5.5): amended `view-boundary.test.ts` plus new turn-end file\\n  - flipped results stay flipped across later turn closes\\n  - short form remains summary-when-ready else truncation\\n  - compact resets boundary to the compact point with a fresh full tail\\n  - same record plus same budgets replays to identical boundary trajectory\\n  - injected `post-commit-advance` failure leaves intake unaffected, boundary unchanged, and status showing over-budget zone\\n  - the next turn close heals the failed advance\\n\\n### Technical Design\\n<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\\n\\n#### Architecture Context\\n\\nThis story patches Epic 03's visibility-boundary contract. The advance registration stays on the existing post-commit seam but is gated to batches that commit a `turn_end`; the decision function changes from message-grained eviction plus floor config to whole-turn groups plus peek-ahead target landing.\\n\\nThe storage shape does not migrate. `view_boundary` remains the stored boundary; `VisibilityBudgets` loses `floorTokens`, and the newest closed turn plus open-turn trigger rule replaces the old floor behavior.\\n\\n#### Build Strategy\\n\\nStrategy: full-staged-risk\\n\\nReason:\\n- This changes a persisted read boundary, replay determinism, config validation, and an existing Epic 03 test surface.\\n- The amendment ledger must be applied precisely so superseded tests are rewritten, not discarded.\\n\\nRisk Reminders:\\n- Keep post-commit ordering and throw isolation unchanged.\\n- Use whole-turn grouping by `turn_id`; turnless results become singleton groups.\\n- Regenerate the red-manifest artifact after ledger amendments.\\n\\n#### Implementation Targets\\n\\n| Area | Files / Modules |\\n|---|---|\\n| Intake post-commit gate | `src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts` |\\n| Boundary decision | `src/domains/thread-view/internal/boundary.ts` |\\n| Visibility config | `src/shared/view.ts`, config resolution code |\\n| Boundary fixtures | `test/fixtures/` boundary helpers including `seedTurnedToolResults(...)` |\\n| Story-owned tests | `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts`, amended `test/view-boundary.test.ts` |\\n| Red-manifest artifact | project red-manifest artifact used by the house Red/Green flow |\\n\\n#### Design References\\n\\n- [epic.md §Flow 5](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/epic.md:151), lines 151-171\\n- [epic.md §Data Contracts](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/epic.md:238), line 238\\n- [tech-design.md §Design Decisions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:28), lines 28-30\\n- [tech-design.md §Top-Tier Surfaces](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:41), lines 41-42\\n- [tech-design.md §Module Responsibility Matrix](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:95), lines 95-97\\n- [tech-design.md §Flow 5](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:175), lines 175-197\\n- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:272), lines 272-275\\n- [test-plan.md §Boundary fixtures](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/test-plan.md:38), line 38\\n- [test-plan.md §TC-5.1 / TC-5.2 / TC-5.3](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/test-plan.md:106), lines 106-125\\n- [test-plan.md §Epic 03 Test Amendment Ledger](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/test-plan.md:138), lines 138-150\\n- [test-plan.md §Red/Green per Chunk](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/test-plan.md:164), line 164\\n- [coverage.md §Story Shape Review](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/coverage.md:77), line 77\\n\\n#### Test Mapping\\n\\n| TC | Test File / Check | Test Description |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| TC-5.1 | `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` | mid-turn batches do not move boundary; turn close advances once; whole oldest turns flip; turnless singleton leg |\\n| TC-5.2 | `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` | G2 peek-ahead landing, exact-target leg, newest-turn protection, `maxTokens > targetTokens`, 64k/32k defaults |\\n| TC-5.3 | amended `test/view-boundary.test.ts` plus new turn-end file | monotonicity, short form, compact reset, deterministic replay, failure injection, next-close heal |\\n\\n#### Architecture-Risk Tests\\n\\n| Risk | Test File / Check | Test Description | Why AC/TC Mapping Alone Would Miss It |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Boundary decision and status sum diverge | amended boundary tests | Status `zoneTokens` and advance decision use the same population after advances and failures | ACs state behavior; this proves two readers do not drift |\\n| Superseded Epic 03 tests deleted wholesale | amendment ledger plus red-manifest regeneration | Each named old leg is inverted, replaced, re-cut, or kept | Green tests alone would not prove the sanctioned test-change path was followed |\\n| Partial-turn eviction | `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` per-turn all-or-nothing assertions | Every tool result in an evicted turn flips together | Boundary position could appear correct while a turn is split internally |\\n\\n#### Technical Notes\\n\\nRelevant contracts:\\n\\n```ts\\nexport interface VisibilityBudgets {\\n  maxTokens: number;\\n  targetTokens: number;\\n}\\n\\n// defaults: { maxTokens: 64_000, targetTokens: 32_000 }\\n// validation: maxTokens > targetTokens\\n```\\n\\nBoundary decision:\\n\\n```text\\nadvanceDecision(groups, { maxTokens, targetTokens }):\\n  total <= maxTokens -> no movement\\n  walk groups oldest-first, stopping before the newest closed turn\\n    (the newest closed turn and any trailing turnless singletons after it\\n     are never candidates; with no closed turn present, exclude the newest\\n     group instead)\\n  evict group only if (remaining - group.tokenSum) >= targetTokens\\n  boundary position = highest source_event_order in last evicted group\\n```\\n\\nGrouping rules:\\n\\n| Case | Grouping |\\n|---|---|\\n| normal turned tool results | group by `turn_id`, oldest first by lowest `source_event_order` |\\n| `turn_id IS NULL` | singleton group |\\n| newest closed turn | never candidate for eviction |\\n| open turn | structurally untouchable because checks only run on turn close |\\n\\nEpic 03 test amendment ledger:\\n\\n| Existing test area | Change | Reason |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| floor-protection legs | superseded and replaced by newest-turn-protection legs in TC-5.2 | `floorTokens` retired |\\n| per-intake-advance legs | inverted into TC-5.1 mid-turn-never-moves assertions | trigger moved to turn close |\\n| message-grained eviction goldens | re-cut for turn grouping | eviction granularity is whole turn |\\n| construction tests passing `floorTokens` | update to two-field budgets; add new rejected-unknown-config test for `floorTokens` | config surface change |\\n| status `zoneTokens` legs | unchanged | shared-query invariant holds |\\n\\nLifecycle/capstone deterministic legs from Epic 04 are untouched. Red-manifest regeneration is required after applying the amendment ledger.\\n\\n#### Transition-State Risk\\n\\n- Mid-turn state may exceed max and remain full until the turn closes.\\n- The open turn is untouchable because no check runs mid-turn.\\n- The newest closed turn is never evicted, even when oversized.\\n- A failed post-commit advance must leave intake committed and status visibly over budget until the next turn close heals it.\\n\\n#### Anti-Shim Requirements\\n\\n- Do not keep a hidden `floorTokens` fallback.\\n- Do not move the advance seam; gate the existing post-commit registration.\\n- Do not evict individual messages from a turned group.\\n- Do not delete Epic 03 tests without applying the ledger and regenerating the red-manifest artifact.\\n\\n#### Production Path Proof\\n\\n- Entrypoint: intake-stream commit pipeline.\\n- Registration/default path: existing post-commit advance registration, gated by committed `turn_end`.\\n- Evidence: turn-end boundary tests assert no mid-turn movement, one advance at close, deterministic replay, and non-blocking failure visibility.\\n\\n#### Verification\\n\\n- Targeted: `cd packages/lhc && pnpm exec vitest run test/view-boundary.test.ts test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts`\\n- Story gate: `cd packages/lhc && pnpm run red-verify && pnpm exec vitest run test/view-boundary.test.ts test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts`\\n- Epic gate: `cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify-all`\\n\\n#### Spec Deviations\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### Definition of Done\\n<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n\\n- Advance registration runs only for batches that committed `turn_end`.\\n- Boundary eviction groups tool results by turn and flips whole groups oldest-first.\\n- Peek-ahead stop and newest-closed-turn protection match TC-5.2.\\n- `floorTokens` is removed from the visibility config surface; defaults and `maxTokens > targetTokens` validation are updated.\\n- Epic 03 amended tests are changed according to the ledger, not deleted wholesale.\\n- Red manifest is regenerated after the test amendments.\\n- TC-5.1, TC-5.2, and TC-5.3 are green.\\n\",\"numLines\":207,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":207}}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/003-quick-fix.stdout.log:36:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_0194868sWkbrABx7G5GRi71s\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"<persisted-output>\\nOutput too large (37.7KB). Full output saved to: /Users/leemoore/.claude/projects/-Users-leemoore-code-pi-long-horizon-liminal-context/c6fd1fc9-717e-4718-8050-43c47347ff45/tool-results/bvpbbpljr.txt\\n\\nPreview (first 2KB):\\n/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/001-story-validate.json\\n/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/004-story-orchestrate-resume.json\\n/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/005-story-orchestrate-resume.json\\n/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/006-implementor.json\\n/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/007-verify.json\\n/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/008-story-orchestrate-resume.json\\n/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/01-cli-retirement/009-story-orchestrate-resume.json\\n/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizo