26-06-12T23:51:58.877Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\" Test Files  40 passed (40)\\n      Tests  376 passed | 9 skipped (385)\\n   Start at  19:51:52\\n   Duration  6.18s (transform 5.48s, setup 0ms, import 27.80s, tests 62.58s, environment 3ms)\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false}}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:2392:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":1,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"viation table including the recorded keyed real-inference run, doc al\"}},\"session_id\":\"bb1f3fcf-4d78-4a97-8c5b-320e502ce14a\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"4b0d4562-f712-4533-af47-4ec61249c32a\"}\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:2394:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"id\":\"msg_01Jmh6rUNpXVkX37CCJM9mJ4\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"All gates pass and the diff is clean. The implementation is complete:\\n\\n- **Trigger gate** (`pipeline.ts`): the advance registration stays at its pinned first-before-poke site, throw-isolated; the callback now consults a flag set only when the walk records a `turn_end` (skipped duplicates never set it).\\n- **Decision reshape** (`boundary.ts`): zone rows carry `turn_id`, group consecutively (NULL → singleton), and the walk evicts whole oldest groups only while the post-eviction sum stays ≥ target; the open turn's group and the newest remaining group are never candidates.\\n- **Config** (`view.ts`/`profiles.ts`): two-field budgets, 64k/32k defaults, `max > target` validation, `floorTokens` rejected as unknown config.\\n- **Tests**: new `view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` (TC-5.1/5.2/5.3, G2 worked golden, exact-target, newest-turn protection, turnless singleton); `view-boundary.test.ts` amended per the ledger; G1 trajectory golden re-cut for turn grouping; ripple amendments in `view-fixture`, `inspect-view`, `view-pull`; red-manifest regenerated; immutability check green.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"ready-for-verification\\\",\\n  \\\"planSummary\\\": \\\"Gated the existing post-commit boundary-advance registration in intake's pipeline on a recorded turn_end (same registration site, ordering, and throw isolation); reshaped the boundary decision to whole-turn groups (turn_id-consecutive grouping, NULL as singleton) with the peek-ahead stop (evict only while remaining ≥ target) and protection for both the open turn's group and the newest remaining group; retired floorTokens from VisibilityBudgets with 64k/32k defaults, max > target validation, and rejection of unknown budget fields; applied the Epic 03 amendment ledger to view-boundary.test.ts and the G1 trajectory golden (re-cut for turn grouping), superseded the floor/monster-turn legs into the new TC-5.2 newest-turn-protection legs, added view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts covering TC-5.1–TC-5.3 including golden G2 (30k/25k/20k/15k under defaults landing the zone at 35k), and regenerated the red manifest. Story gate (verify) and epic gate (verify-all) both pass: 40 files, 376 passed, 9 env-gated skips.\\\",\\n  \\\"changedFiles\\\": [\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"AC-5.1: advance registration gated on a recorded turn_end via a walk-set flag; registration site, advance-before-poke order, and throw isolation untouched\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/boundary.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"AC-5.1–5.3: zone read gains turn_id, groupZone builds whole-turn eviction units, advanceDecision becomes the peek-ahead whole-group walk excluding the open turn's group and the newest candidate group\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"AC-5.4: VisibilityBudgets reduced to { maxTokens, targetTokens }; default comment updated to 64000/32000\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"AC-5.4: DEFAULT_VISIBILITY 64000/32000, floor validation removed, unknown budget fields (floorTokens) rejected at construction with a TypeError naming the field\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"New story-owned suite: TC-5.1 (turn-end trigger, byte-stable mid-turn pulls, exactly-one-advance counting, whole-turn all-or-nothing, turnless singleton), TC-5.2 (golden G2 under 64k/32k defaults, exact-target ≥ leg, oversized-newest protection, max ≤ target TypeError, defaults), TC-5.3 (replay determinism + forward-only)\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/test/view-boundary.test.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"Amendment ledger applied: per-intake legs re-cut for turn grouping, old TC-4.3 floor legs superseded (note left pointing at TC-5.2), construction tests moved to two-field budgets plus the floorTokens-rejected leg, TC-4.6 heal re-cut to multi-turn batches, seam-direction-two re-cut to the 64k/32k defaults; status zoneTokens assertions kept (shared-query invariant)\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/test/goldens/boundary-g1-trajectory.json\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"G1 re-cut for turn grouping and turn-end trigger: 6 batches covering under-max closes, whole-turn eviction with peek-ahead, no-move close, mid-turn over-max hold, and the healing close that evicts three groups\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/test/view-select-golden.test.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"BoundaryGolden budgets type reduced to two fields; G1 comments updated to the turn-end contract (replay-equality leg unchanged)\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/test/goldens/README.md\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"boundary-g1-trajectory row updated to describe the re-cut rule set\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/view-boundary.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"New boundary fixture: boundaryTokens/boundaryToolRun/turnedToolResultEvents/seedTurnedToolResults — scripted closed/open/turnless turns seeded through real intake commits\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/index.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"Re-export the new boundary fixture helpers\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/test/view-fixture.test.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"Construction legs: target<floor leg replaced by floorTokens-unknown rejection; defaults assertion updated to 64000/32000\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/test/inspect-view.test.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"Boundary-advanced fixture leg: floorTokens dropped from small budgets (same expected positions under turn grouping); comment updated\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"Status leg's default maxTokens expectation 32000 → 64000 (downstream of AC-5.4 defaults)\\\" },\\n    { \\\"path\\\": \\\"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\\\", \\\"reason\\\": \\\"Regenerated hashes for the amended/new Red-phase files after applying the amendment ledger\\\" }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tests\\\": {\\n    \\\"added\\\": [\\n      \\\"test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts (9 tests: TC-5.1 trigger/whole-turn/turnless legs, TC-5.2 G2/exact-target/newest-protection/oversized-loner/validation/defaults legs, TC-5.3 replay-determinism leg)\\\",\\n      \\\"test/view-boundary.test.ts: floorTokens-rejected-as-unknown-config leg (ledger-sanctioned new construction test)\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"modified\\\": [\\n      \\\"test/view-boundary.test.ts (TC-4.1/4.4/4.6, seam-direction-two, deleted-filter, both-modes re-cut for turn grouping and turn-end trigger; TC-4.5 two-field)\\\",\\n      \\\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts (BoundaryGolden type + G1 comments)\\\",\\n      \\\"test/goldens/boundary-g1-trajectory.json (re-cut trajectory)\\\",\\n      \\\"test/view-fixture.test.ts (validation + defaults legs)\\\",\\n      \\\"test/inspect-view.test.ts (two-field small budgets)\\\",\\n      \\\"test/view-pull.test.ts (default maxTokens 64000)\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"removed\\\": [\\n      \\\"test/view-boundary.test.ts old TC-4.3 legs (monster open turn entered by the advance; oversized-newest floor protection) — superseded per the amendment ledger by TC-5.1 mid-turn untouchability and TC-5.2 newest-turn-protection legs\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"totalAfterStory\\\": 376,\\n    \\\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\\\": 7\\n  },\\n  \\\"gatesRun\\\": [\\n    { \\\"command\\\": \\\"cd packages/lhc && pnpm run typecheck\\\", \\\"result\\\": \\\"pass\\\" },\\n    { \\\"command\\\": \\\"cd packages/lhc && pnpm exec vitest run test/view-boundary.test.ts test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts test/view-select-golden.test.ts\\\", \\\"result\\\": \\\"pass\\\" },\\n    { \\\"command\\\": \\\"cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify\\\", \\\"result\\\": \\\"pass\\\" },\\n    { \\\"command\\\": \\\"cd packages/lhc && node scripts/check-test-immutability.mjs (after red-manifest regeneration)\\\", \\\"result\\\": \\\"pass\\\" },\\n    { \\\"command\\\": \\\"cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify-all\\\", \\\"result\\\": \\\"pass\\\" }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"selfReview\\\": {\\n    \\\"findingsFixed\\\": [\\n      \\\"G1 B6 walk arithmetic initially mis-derived (two evictions); re-derived by hand to three group evictions (t2, t3, t4) landing at order 21 with zone 80 before committing the golden\\\",\\n      \\\"New-suite close-only batch was built through an awkward fixture filter; replaced with a bare validEvent(\\\\\\\"turn_end\\\\\\\") batch, which also exercises the close-only-batch trigger path\\\",\\n      \\\"TC-4.6's heal leg could never heal under whole-turn eviction with its original single 120-token turn (evicting it would land below target); re-cut to three single-result turns so the peek-ahead admits an eviction\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"findingsSurfaced\\\": [\\n      \\\"advanceDecision excludes the open turn's group explicitly in addition to the newest candidate group: the design's 'exclude the newest group' alone would let a batch that commits a turn_end and then opens a new turn with tool results evict the newest CLOSED turn, violating AC-5.3; the explicit exclusion makes the open-turn untouchability structural rather than assumed\\\",\\n      \\\"A turn closed by close_then_open (a new user_prompt) does not run the advance check — AC-5.1 names committed turn_end as the only trigger; the G1 golden's B5/B6 legs document that the next committed turn_end heals such a close\\\",\\n      \\\"The gate counts only recorded turn_end events: a batch whose turn_end is skipped as a duplicate idempotency key triggers nothing, consistent with 'commits a turn_end'\\\",\\n      \\\"test/view-pull.test.ts's status leg (default maxTokens) is downstream of the AC-5.4 default change but is not named in the amendment ledger; amended (32000 → 64000) and recorded in the regenerated red-manifest\\\"\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \\\"openQuestions\\\": [],\\n  \\\"specDeviations\\\": [\\n    \\\"seedTurnedToolResults is implemented as (sdk, filePath, turns) seeding through a real intake commit, not the test plan's sketched (db, turns) signature: a direct-DB seeder could never fire the production advance (no host-called advance surface exists, per the inherited anti-shim rule), so the fixture drives the production path instead\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"recommendedNextStep\\\": \\\"Story verification pass, then epic-level review: with Story 6 done all six stories of Epic 05 are implemented, so the epic closeout (deviation table including the recorded keyed real-inference run, doc alignment, final gate) is next\\\"\\n}\\n```\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1683,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":175313,\"cache_creation\":{\"ep