 amendment ledger to view-boundary.test.ts and the G1 trajectory golden (re-cut for turn grouping), superseded the floor/monster-turn legs into the new TC-5.2 newest-turn-protection legs, added view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts covering TC-5.1–TC-5.3 including golden G2 (30k/25k/20k/15k under defaults landing the zone at 35k), and regenerated the red manifest. Story gate (verify) and epic gate (verify-all) both pass: 40 files, 376 passed, 9 env-gated skips.\",\"acceptanceRationale\":\"Story-lead is pausing for caller ruling 06-turn-end-boundary-advance-story-run-001-ruling-020 before impl-lead can accept the story.\"},\"evidence\":{\"implementorArtifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"implementor-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/003-implementor.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"}],\"selfReviewArtifacts\":[],\"verifierArtifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"verifier-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/004-verify.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"},{\"kind\":\"verifier-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/005-verify.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"}],\"quickFixArtifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"quick-fix-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/quick-fix/002-quick-fix.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"}],\"callerInputArtifacts\":[],\"gateRuns\":[{\"command\":\"cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}]},\"verification\":{\"finalVerifierOutcome\":\"block\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"F-06-002\",\"status\":\"unresolved\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/005-verify.json\",\"AC-5.3 still says the advance lands in `[target, target + one turn)`. The new trailing-turnless TC-5.2 leg in `view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` uses budgets 100/60 with groups t1=50, newest closed t2=45, trailing turnless=70, then expects boundary after t1 and `zoneTokens` 115. If the next protected turn is the newest closed turn, the AC window is `[60, 105)`, so the expected 115 is outside it. This is not a code failure in the quick fix; it exposes a product/spec ruling needed for the legal trailing-turnless shape because a scalar boundary cannot both skip the trailing singleton and preserve the newest closed turn. The story technical notes were changed to protect trailing turnless singletons after the newest closed turn, but the AC wording and tech-design.md Flow 5 still carry the general landing-window phrasing.\"]}]},\"riskAndDeviationReview\":{\"specDeviations\":[{\"description\":\"seedTurnedToolResults is implemented as (sdk, filePath, turns) seeding through a real intake commit, not the test plan's sketched (db, turns) signature: a direct-DB seeder could never fire the production advance (no host-called advance surface exists, per the inherited anti-shim rule), so the fixture drives the production path instead\",\"reasoning\":\"Story implementor surfaced this spec deviation during bounded child execution.\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/003-implementor.json\"],\"approvalStatus\":\"needs-ruling\",\"approvalSource\":null}],\"assumedRisks\":[],\"scopeChanges\":[],\"productionPathDecisionItems\":[{\"description\":\"No fake adapter, shim, placeholder branch, hidden floorTokens fallback, or non-real