ess shape because a scalar boundary cannot both skip the trailing singleton and preserve the newest closed turn. The story technical notes were changed to protect trailing turnless singletons after the newest closed turn, but the AC wording and tech-design.md Flow 5 still carry the general landing-window phrasing.\"]}],\"baselineBeforeStory\":369,\"baselineAfterStory\":376,\"openRisks\":[\"Verification finding F-06-002 remains unresolved.\",\"Verification finding F-06-002 remains unresolved.\"]},\"cumulativeBaseline\":{\"baselineBeforeCurrentStory\":369,\"expectedAfterCurrentStory\":376,\"latestActualTotal\":376},\"commitReadiness\":{\"state\":\"not-ready\",\"reason\":\"Caller ruling is still required before impl-lead commit.\"},\"openRisks\":[\"Verification finding F-06-002 remains unresolved.\",\"Verification finding F-06-002 remains unresolved.\"]},\"cleanupHandoff\":{\"acceptedRiskItems\":[],\"deferredItems\":[{\"description\":\"No fake adapter, shim, placeholder branch, hidden floorTokens fallback, or non-real boundary advance surface was found in the reviewed production files.\",\"reasoning\":\"Story verifier surfaced a production-path audit note. Verifier outcome, open findings, and explicit story-lead risk decisions determine whether action or caller approval is required.\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/06-turn-end-boundary-advance/005-verify.json\",\"No fake adapter, shim, placeholder branch, hidden floorTokens fallback, or non-real boundary advance surface was found in the reviewed production files.\"],\"approvalStatus\":\"not-required\",\"approvalSource\":null},{\"description\":\"The prior production-path bug is fixed, but the trailing-turnless shape now exposes an unresolved AC-5.3 landing-window