{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/coverage.md | sed -n '1,180p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Epic 05 Story Coverage\n     2\t\n     3\t## Coverage Gate\n     4\t\n     5\tEvery AC and TC has exactly one primary owner story.\n     6\t\n     7\t| ID | Primary owner | Coverage |\n     8\t|---|---|---|\n     9\t| AC-1.1 | Story 2 | `createSdk` provider XOR inference |\n    10\t| AC-1.2 | Story 2 | `ModelCall` contract |\n    11\t| AC-1.3 | Story 2 | complete assignment validation |\n    12\t| AC-1.4 | Story 2 | per-call routing |\n    13\t| TC-1.1 | Story 2 | construction matrix |\n    14\t| TC-1.2 | Story 2 | routing and fake-host contract assertions |\n    15\t| AC-2.1 | Story 3 | seven adapter operations |\n    16\t| AC-2.2 | Story 3 | prompt rendering and mechanical facts |\n    17\t| AC-2.3 | Story 3 | named/versioned prompts |\n    18\t| AC-2.4 | Story 3 | empty-output failure |\n    19\t| AC-2.5 | Story 3 | provenance metadata |\n    20\t| TC-2.1 | Story 3 | seven ready forms, facts, provenance |\n    21\t| TC-2.2 | Story 3 | prompt goldens and input stripping/bounding |\n    22\t| TC-2.3 | Story 3 | whitespace output failure |\n    23\t| AC-3.1 | Story 4 | fixed classification table |\n    24\t| AC-3.2 | Story 4 | retry/terminal machinery |\n    25\t| AC-3.3 | Story 4 | thrown exception containment |\n    26\t| TC-3.1 | Story 4 | retryable, terminal, exhaustion |\n    27\t| TC-3.2 | Story 4 | throw and timeout containment |\n    28\t| AC-4.1 | Story 5 | real-suite ran/not-ran accounting and real host |\n    29\t| AC-4.2 | Story 5 | real-adapter capstone |\n    30\t| TC-4.1 | Story 5 | real round-trips and accounting |\n    31\t| TC-4.2 | Story 5 | lifecycle capstone |\n    32\t| TC-4.3 | Story 5 | real-host contract conformance |\n    33\t| AC-5.1 | Story 6 | turn-end-only trigger |\n    34\t| AC-5.2 | Story 6 | whole-turn eviction |\n    35\t| AC-5.3 | Story 6 | peek-ahead landing and newest-turn protection |\n    36\t| AC-5.4 | Story 6 | two-field config and validation |\n    37\t| AC-5.5 | Story 6 | Epic 03 contracts under new trigger |\n    38\t| TC-5.1 | Story 6 | turn-end trigger and whole-turn eviction |\n    39\t| TC-5.2 | Story 6 | peek-ahead and config |\n    40\t| TC-5.3 | Story 6 | Epic 03 regression legs |\n    41\t| AC-6.1 | Story 1 | CLI deletion and SDK-only exports |\n    42\t| AC-6.2 | Story 1 | process-suite deletion without weakened SDK tests |\n    43\t| AC-6.3 | Story 1 | env/flag provider resolution gone |\n    44\t| TC-6.1 | Story 1 | deletion proof |\n    45\t| TC-6.2 | Story 1 | resolution path gone |\n    46\t\n    47\tGate result: pass. 22 ACs and 15 TCs are mapped; no unmapped or double-primary items.\n    48\t\n    49\t## Integration Path Trace\n    50\t\n    51\t| Path segment | Story | TC owner | Assertion |\n    52\t|---|---|---|---|\n    53\t| SDK-only provider arrival after CLI deletion | Story 1 | TC-6.1, TC-6.2 | package has no binary; registry exports and env/flag resolution are gone |\n    54\t| Host supplies inference config | Story 2 | TC-1.1 | exactly one of `provider` / `inference`; complete assignments required |\n    55\t| Work item routes to assigned lane | Story 2 | TC-1.2 | each kind calls its configured provider/model with single-turn messages |\n    56\t| Adapter renders prompt and lands content | Story 3 | TC-2.1, TC-2.2 | seven kinds render prompts and produce ready forms |\n    57\t| Mechanical facts remain record-authored | Story 3 | TC-2.1, TC-2.2 | outcomes/receipts and brief-summary stripping hold under real adapter |\n    58\t| Empty success output does not become ready | Story 3 | TC-2.3 | whitespace classifies as `empty_output` and follows retry budget |\n    59\t| Structured and thrown failures enter queue machinery | Story 4 | TC-3.1, TC-3.2 | retryable, terminal, timeout, and thrown cases do not fork queue behavior |\n    60\t| Real endpoint exercises same seam | Story 5 | TC-4.1, TC-4.3 | OpenRouter host conforms to `ModelCall` and routing helpers |\n    61\t| Real adapter completes lifecycle capstone | Story 5 | TC-4.2 | all derivations ready with real provenance and coherent checkpoints |\n    62\t| Visibility boundary advances at turn close | Story 6 | TC-5.1 | mid-turn reads remain byte-identical; turn close advances once |\n    63\t| Boundary eviction respects whole turns and target landing | Story 6 | TC-5.2 | groups flip whole-turn oldest-first and land in target range |\n    64\t| Epic 03 boundary contracts survive trigger move | Story 6 | TC-5.3 | forward-only, short form, compact reset, deterministic replay, and failure visibility hold |\n    65\t\n    66\tTrace result: pass. All six flows have story and TC ownership.\n    67\t\n    68\t## Story Shape Review\n    69\t\n    70\t| Story | Type | Governing idea | Overload flags | Risk flags | Split decision |\n    71\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n    72\t| 1. CLI Retirement | packaging / deletion | Public API becomes SDK-only before inference plumbing starts. | none | public API break, suite deletion | Keep: deletion surface is one coherent retirement. |\n    73\t| 2. Inference Seam and Model Assignment | foundation / invariant | `createSdk` construction is the single validated source of inference routing. | none | construction validation, cross-story contract change | Keep: all ACs define one boundary contract. |\n    74\t| 3. Adapter and Seven Prompts | adapter / mapping | The adapter turns each derivation kind into prompt-rendered model text without moving domain handlers. | multiple semantic operations | prompt fidelity, source/derived metadata, fixture fidelity | Keep: one `DerivationProvider` implementation owns all seven operations. |\n    75\t| 4. Failure Classification | semantic rule | Model-call failures map by a fixed table into existing retry/terminal behavior. | none | retry semantics, timeout containment | Keep: classification is one table plus containment wrapper. |\n    76\t| 5. Real-Inference Suite and Capstone | fixture / packaging + capstone integration | The same host function seam is proven against a real endpoint and lifecycle exercise. | capstone plus seam conformance | auth-gated run, external endpoint, capstone integration | Keep: suite accounting is inseparable from real endpoint proof. |\n    77\t| 6. Turn-End Boundary Advance | semantic rule / contract patch | Visibility boundary movement is turn-close-owned and whole-turn-grained. | config change plus regression amendments | transition-state atomicity, replay determinism, Epic 03 test amendments | Keep: trigger, grouping, config, and amendments are one boundary contract change. |\n    78\t\n    79\tShape result: pass. No story has unresolved overload flags.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
