{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_0132bGe9BM3MTeHuFhuFccgx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All checks are complete. The epic gate is green (40 files, 377 passed, 9 env-gated keyed legs skipped with visible NOT-RAN accounting), the keyed integration run is recorded in the impl log, the production path contains no fakes or placeholders, and the implementation matches the tech design across all six flows.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n  \"crossStoryFindings\": [\n    \"Story 2 → Story 3 seam handoff is coherent: createSdk's resolveInferenceProvider (src/sdk.ts:313-359) validates XOR, all seven FORM_KINDS (iterating the exported union per the Chunk-2 risk note, never a literal list), unknown kind keys, non-empty provider/model strings, and PROMPT_REGISTRY membership, then drops the adapter into the same resolved.provider slot direct injection uses — everything downstream is unchanged Epic 02 code.\",\n    \"Story 3 → Story 4 reason-format coupling is consistent and ruling-backed: the adapter formats retryable reasons as 'provider_failure: <kind>: <message>' and terminal reasons kind-led (src/inference/adapter.ts:47-55); the team-impl-log records the approved spec-deviation ruling for this format, and Story 4's classification tests consume the same format. The queue (failAttempt/failTerminal in src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts:350-417) copies the reason verbatim at exhaustion, so forms land with the 'provider_failure'-led reason AC-3.2 requires under the established code-before-first-colon convention.\",\n    \"Story 4's machinery-untouched claim verified: FAILURE_CLASSIFICATION and safeCall live entirely in src/inference/classify.ts; the work-queue's failAttempt/failTerminal retain their Epic 02 shape (retryable backoff within budget, terminal immediate, attempts/lastError copied to form metadata) with no inference-aware branches.\",\n    \"Story 5 reuses Story 2's seam-conformance helpers parameterized over both hosts per DD-13: test/inference-real.test.ts runs assertModelCallContract and assertRoutingThroughSdk (the same helpers the fake-host tests run) against the OpenRouter host unchanged.\",\n    \"Story 6 (boundary) and Story 1 (retirement) are cleanly independent of the inference pipeline as designed; the pipeline gate (src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:152-168, 219) keeps the Epic 03 registration site, advance-before-poke order, and throw isolation untouched while gating on a batchCommittedTurnEnd flag that skipped duplicate turn_end events never set.\",\n    \"Provenance flows one direction across stories: stamped from config-known strings in the adapter (src/inference/adapter.ts:91-99), copied — never authored — by the messages handler (src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts:61-72) and all three turns-side form writes (src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:101-104, 122-124, 201-203); the deterministic provider sets none (src/providers/deterministic.ts).\"\n  ],\n  \"architectureFindings\": [\n    \"Module architecture matches the tech design exactly: src/inference/{types,classify,adapter,prompts/*} exist as specified; the seven prompt modules are name-keyed in PROMPT_REGISTRY with versioned names; smoothing-v1 is marked SETTLED (POC port) and the other six carry PRE-DIAL-IN markers per AC-2.3.\",\n    \"The inference/ ↛ domains/ boundary rule was added to scripts/check-boundaries.mjs (lines 117-155) as the tech design required; inference/ imports only shared/ types, and the shared/derivation.ts → inference/types.ts import is type-only and documented as erased at build, keeping the runtime graph one-directional.\",\n    \"DD-6/DD-7 resolved as designed: safeCall owns the per-call timeout (Promise.race with timer cleanup, default 60_000) classifying as retryable 'timeout'; input bounding for summarizeToolResult is head-and-tail with marker under maxInputChars (default 200_000), applied before prompt rendering, with a correct degenerate path when the bound is smaller than the marker itself.\",\n    \"Flow 5 implementation matches the design's conditional landing-window contract: advanceDecision (src/domains/thread-view/internal/boundary.ts:157-195) is a pure function with whole-turn grouping (NULL turn_id degrading to singleton groups per DD-10), peek-ahead stop (remaining − group ≥ target), open-turn exclusion from candidacy while its tokens count in the sum, and newest-closed-turn protection that structurally protects trailing turnless singletons; the shared-WHERE-clause invariant between visibilityZoneTokens and readZoneToolResults holds, and the forward-only guard is in the UPDATE itself.\",\n    \"AC-5.4 lands fully: VisibilityBudgets is two-field with 64000/32000 defaults (src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts:35-38), maxTokens > targetTokens validated with a naming TypeError, and the retired floorTokens is explicitly rejected as unknown config with a message citing the Epic 05 retirement.\",\n    \"Construction error contract matches §Error Contract: all violations are TypeErrors naming the violated rule ('exactly one of provider or inference', 'missing kind <kind>', 'names unknown template', 'maxTokens must be greater than targetTokens').\"\n  ],\n  \"epicCoverageAssessment\": [\n    \"All 22 ACs across 6 flows trace to implementation and tests. Flow 1: TC-1.1 parameterizes the construction matrix over FORM_KINDS (test/inference-construction.test.ts:64); TC-1.2 routing via recordingCall lanes. Flow 2: TC-2.1 includes the adversarial wrong-outcome canned text (test/inference-adapter.test.ts:45-49, 142); TC-2.2 goldens exist for all seven templates (test/goldens/prompts/); TC-2.3 empty-output retry and exhaustion legs present. Flow 3: TC-3.1 asserts FAILURE_CLASSIFICATION as data matching AC-3.1 exactly; TC-3.2 covers thrown-exception containment and the hangingCall timeout leg. Flow 5: golden G2 implemented verbatim (30k/25k/20k/15k under 64k/32k landing at 35k), exact-target boundary condition, oversized-newest protection, and the trailing-turnless-singleton protection leg. Flow 6: retirement.test.ts proves the export snapshot, no bin, deleted files, and zero LHC_PROVIDER/--provider references with the retired env var actively set.\",\n    \"Epic gate verify-all exits 0: 40 test files, 377 passed, 9 skipped — the 9 skips are exactly the env-gated keyed legs (2 round-trip/conformance + 7 capstone), with the single visible 'NOT-RAN: real-inference (LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY unset)' accounting line per AC-4.1.\",\n    \"The test plan's epic-acceptance condition for the capstone is satisfied: the team-impl-log records the DoD keyed-run receipt — date 2026-06-12, model openai/gpt-5.4-mini, 13/13 pass, exactly one 'RAN: real-inference' accounting line, run twice — so the integration-readiness gate (AC-4.2) has actually been exercised against a real endpoint, not just defined.\",\n    \"The Epic 03 amendment ledger was applied (view-boundary.test.ts amended for two-field budgets, mid-turn-never-moves inversions, re-cut G1; floorTokens-rejection test added in view-fixture.test.ts) and the red-manifest regenerated per the Story 6 commit.\",\n    \"The Epic 04 parity-gap deviation note required by Flow 6 is recorded in the team-impl-log (spawned inspect-health parity backfilled pre-Epic-05; spawned-process parity surface deleted instead of carried forward).\"\n  ],\n  \"productionPathFindings\": [\n    \"No fake adapters, shims, or placeholders in the production path. src/ contains zero TODO/FIXME/not-implemented markers (the only 'placeholder' hits are SQL bind-parameter builders), zero process.env reads, and zero fetch calls — the production path is fully real, and all network code lives in the test-owned OpenRouter fixture as the NFR requires.\",\n    \"All scripted/recording/throwing/hanging ModelCall fakes live in test/fixtures/model-call.ts (test code), which is the spec-designated mock boundary for Flows 1–3 — boundary mocks, not internal mocks, per the testing strategy.\",\n    \"The deterministic marker-string provider survives only as the explicitly-injected CI test provider (src/providers/deterministic.ts, DD-12); it cannot arrive silently — provider arrival is strict XOR injection at createSdk with no defaults, no registry, and no env fallback (verified by retirement.test.ts with LHC_PROVIDER actively set in the environment).\",\n    \"The OpenRouter ModelCall host is test-owned by design (DD-13, AC-4.1) — it is the proof-of-seam second host, not a production shim; the production host (PI extension) is explicitly out of scope for this epic.\",\n    \"The adapter's empty-output rule is enforced in the production path (whitespace-trimmed text rejected as retryable empty_output before any form can land ready), and provenance is mechanically copied from config strings, never parsed from model output.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockingFindings\": [],\n  \"nonBlockingFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E05-NB-1\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"verify and verify-all are now textually identical scripts\",\n      \"evidence\": \"package.json defines both 'verify' and 'verify-all' as 'pnpm run red-verify && vitest run'. The convergence is spec-sanctioned (the process-suite gate left verify-all and the inference suite is env-gated inside the default runner), but two independently-maintained identical definitions can drift apart silently; aliasing one to the other would pin the intent.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/lhc/package.json\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-6.2\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E05-NB-2\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Prompt names are config-selectable strings with no exported name catalog\",\n      \"evidence\": \"PROMPT_REGISTRY and DEFAULT_PROMPT_NAMES (src/inference/prompts/index.ts) are construction internals not exported from the package entry (the retirement snapshot confirms the SDK-only surface). A host must learn valid prompt names from documentation; unknown names fail construction loudly per AC-1.3, so the fail-loudly posture holds, but the PI extension PRD should account for how operators discover the seven default names.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/index.ts\", \"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-1.3\", \"AC-2.3\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E05-NB-3\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"title\": \"Turn-derivation work item re-runs the rendering call when only the projection fails\",\n      \"evidence\": \"turnDerivationHandler (src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:85-88) makes two sequential provider calls (composeTurnRendering then projectLowerBand) in one work item; a retryable projection failure retries the whole item, re-invoking the rendering call. This is pre-existing Epic 02 work-item granularity, but under real inference each retry now costs a redundant real model call, bounded by the retry budget. Worth weighing during dial-in if projection failures prove common.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-3.2\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E05-NB-4\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Real-suite gating uses describe.runIf skips alongside the single accounting line\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The test plan said the accounting rule is 'a suite-level guard, not per-test skips'; the implementation resolves the env once at module load and emits exactly one line (the guard), but the keyed legs surface as 9 vitest 'skipped' entries via describe.runIf. The run/not-run state remains one fact reported once and the skips add runner-level visibility rather than hiding anything, so the AC-4.1 intent is met; noting the cosmetic divergence from the plan's wording.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/lhc/test/inference-real.test.ts\", \"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/openrouter-call.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-4.1\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"same-session-implementor\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E05-NB-5\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Epic document status header still reads Draft\",\n      \"evidence\": \"docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/epic.md line 3 reads 'Status: Draft — pending review' while all six stories are implemented, gated, and logged complete. The pack also carries the planned pre-acceptance backfill dependency (dial-in findings), so the header may be intentional, but it should be reconciled at acceptance.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/epic.md\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolvedItems\": [\n    \"Prompt/model dial-in findings are an explicit pre-acceptance backfill obligation for this pack (epic §Out of Scope, tech design §Deferred Items) — plumbing is proven but the tuned prompts and model assignments do not exist yet by design.\",\n    \"The capstone keyed run was executed locally and recorded in the impl log (2026-06-12, openai/gpt-5.4-mini, 13/13); it cannot gate CI by design (no secret in CI), so future regressions in the keyed path are detectable only by re-running the keyed suite manually.\"\n  ],\n  \"gateResult\": \"pass\"\n}\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1800,"cache_read_input_tokens":128000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1800},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management