nternals not exported from the package entry (the retirement snapshot confirms the SDK-only surface). A host must learn valid prompt names from documentation; unknown names fail construction loudly per AC-1.3, so the fail-loudly posture holds, but the PI extension PRD should account for how operators discover the seven default names.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/lhc/src/inference/prompts/index.ts\", \"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-1.3\", \"AC-2.3\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E05-NB-3\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"title\": \"Turn-derivation work item re-runs the rendering call when only the projection fails\",\n      \"evidence\": \"turnDerivationHandler (src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:85-88) makes two sequential provider calls (composeTurnRendering then projectLowerBand) in one work item; a retryable projection failure retries the whole item, re-invoking the rendering call. This is pre-existing Epic 02 work-item granularity, but under real inference each retry now costs a redundant real model call, bounded by the retry budget. Worth weighing during dial-in if projection failures prove common.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-3.2\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E05-NB-4\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Real-suite gating uses describe.runIf skips alongside the single accounting line\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The test plan said the accounting rule is 'a suite-level guard, not per-test skips'; the implementation resolves the env once at module load and emits exactly one line (the guard), but the keyed legs surface as 9 vitest 'skipped' entries via describe.runIf. The run/not-run state remains one fact reported once and the skips add runner-level visibility rather than hiding anything, so the AC-4.1 intent is met; noting the cosmetic divergence from the plan's wording.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/lhc/test/inference-real.test.ts\", \"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/openrouter-call.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-4.1\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"same-session-implementor\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E05-NB-5\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Epic document status header still reads Draft\",\n      \"evidence\": \"docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/epic.md line 3 reads 'Status: Draft — pending review' while all six stories are implemented, gated, and logged complete. The pack also carries the planned pre-acceptance backfill dependency (dial-in findings), so the header may be intentional, but it should be reconciled at acceptance.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/epic.md\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolvedItems\": [\n    \"Prompt/model dial-in findings are an explicit pre-acceptance backfill obligation for this pack (epic §Out of Scope, tech design §Deferred Items) — plumbing is proven but the tuned prompts and model assignments do not exist yet by design.\",\n    \"The capstone keyed run was executed locally and recorded in the impl log (2026-06-12, openai/gpt-5.4-mini, 13/13); it cannot gate CI by design (no secret in CI), so future regressions in the keyed path are detectable only by re-running the keyed suite manually.\"\n  ],\n  \"gateResult\": \"pass\"\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"bfcb3770-4909-4548-8bb4-e503f40f13df","total_cost_usd":4.802135999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2685,"cache_creation_input_tokens":108336,"cache_read_input_tokens":1513314,"output_tokens":21874,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"ser